<BaseLayout
	title="Now"
	description="What Arnold Gamboa is focused on right now — day job, church, YouPastor, and writing."
	path="/now/"
>
	<article class="page">
		<p class="meta-line">Last updated · May 2026 · Pasig City, Philippines</p>
		<h1>Now</h1>
		<p class="page__lede">
			A single page for what I’m focused on at this point in my life — not a resume, not a
			roadmap.
		</p>

		<p>
			I’m in a narrowing season. A few months ago I had several things moving at once:
			ChurchPrompt.Directory, ReguBrief, ArwenHQ, agency work, AI coding experiments, and
			whatever else looked interesting enough to build. Most of that is paused now. Not
			abandoned. Just paused.
		</p>
		<p>
			The thing taking most of my attention outside of my day job and church life is{' '}
			<a href="https://youpastor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouPastor</a>.
			I’m trying to get it ready for launch soon. It’s been forcing me to think less like
			someone who likes building tools and more like someone who has to choose what actually
			matters. That’s been good for me. A little uncomfortable, but good.
		</p>
		<p>
			I’m still writing when I can — mostly about AI, software, pastors, and what happens when
			tools move from novelty to actual weekly work.
		</p>
		<p>
			At church, I’m still preaching, leading, and carrying the normal rhythms of ministry.
			That context is part of why YouPastor exists in the first place.
		</p>
		<p>
			So that’s the honest update: fewer projects, more focus, and one main thing for now.
		</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
